ded equivalent local endpoint; requests in the same sequence stay pinned to that endpoint; route-status/session evidence expose sticky and utilization facts; multi-machine correctness is tracked separately through shared lease design. This epic owns decomposition only; child beads carry implementation scope and acceptance.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\n1. All child beads are closed with evidence. 2. docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-003-providers.md and FEAT-004-model-routing.md include acceptance criteria for provider-owned vLLM/llama-server utilization, go-vcr real-server cassettes, sticky same-key routing, and different-key load distribution. 3. go test ./... passes after implementation beads land.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:routing, kind:epic\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata spec-id=\"FEAT-004\" base-rev=\"d9d912801092c5fd3d7479051d06de076732009d\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260506T003958-18c8dca3\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cref id=\"FEAT-004\" path=\"docs/helix/01-frame/features/FEAT-004-model-routing.md\"\u003eFeature Specification: FEAT-004 — Shared Model Catalog, Power-Based Routing, and Provider Configuration\u003c/ref\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"attempt_id":"20260506T003958-18c8dca3","base_rev":"d9d912801092c5fd3d7479051d06de076732009d","bead_id":"fizeau-c58969b6","bundle_path":".ddx/executions/20260506T003958-18c8dca3","correlation_id":"fizeau-c58969b6:20260506T003958-18c8dca3","prompt_file":".ddx/executions/20260506T003958-18c8dca3/prompt.md","prompt_sha":"1f7b4f675469076a5bcb966293da12cd4b7793bef019efe228e1e95c9f8b2019","role":"implementer","session_id":"eb-533b1a2f","worker_id":""}}}
